  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345156",
      "title": "Creating React Projects",
      "sourceHash": "eb33b2cb0a22ee3150a51157d1333f4ad3cf86ca4964440eafde0381a972757a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.21,
          "end": 3.18,
          "en": "So now that you know what's in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.18,
          "end": 7.44,
          "en": "and you know which paths you can take to complete the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.44,
          "end": 11.58,
          "en": "and you know how you can get the most out of this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.58,
          "end": 14.79,
          "en": "let's finally get started with React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.79,
          "end": 17.34,
          "en": "and with writing React code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 21.81,
          "en": "And for that, of course, you typically need a React project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.81,
          "end": 24.3,
          "en": "where you can write that code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.3,
          "end": 27.75,
          "en": "And whilst you'll learn how to write React code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.75,
          "end": 30.45,
          "en": "and which React features you should know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.45,
          "end": 32.97,
          "en": "in the next course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.97,
          "end": 36.69,
          "en": "it's this lecture here where I wanna show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.69,
          "end": 40.38,
          "en": "how you can create React projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.38,
          "end": 43.53,
          "en": "And one of the quickest ways of getting started",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.53,
          "end": 45.81,
          "en": "with writing React code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.81,
          "end": 50.81,
          "en": "is to type react.new into your browser URL bar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.96,
          "end": 53.67,
          "en": "And if you then hit Enter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.67,
          "end": 58.67,
          "en": "a brand new React project workspace will be created for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.64,
          "end": 63.36,
          "en": "with help of a website called CodeSandbox,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.36,
          "end": 68.22,
          "en": "which gives you an in-browser development environment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.22,
          "end": 71.82,
          "en": "so that you can work on files and write code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 71.82,
          "end": 75.63,
          "en": "and see a review of the website you are working on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.63,
          "end": 80.63,
          "en": "in the browser without installing anything locally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 81.03,
          "end": 82.53,
          "en": "And that's therefore, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.53,
          "end": 85.53,
          "en": "a great choice to get started quickly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.53,
          "end": 87.33,
          "en": "and also a great choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.33,
          "end": 91.17,
          "en": "if you simply can't install software locally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.17,
          "end": 92.82,
          "en": "because you're maybe working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.82,
          "end": 95.43,
          "en": "on a computer issued by a company",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.43,
          "end": 98.37299999999999,
          "en": "that doesn't give you administrator permissions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.50999999999999,
          "end": 101.72999999999999,
          "en": "And indeed, throughout the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.72999999999999,
          "end": 104.19,
          "en": "in all those course sections,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 107.91,
          "en": "I will always provide you with starting projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.91,
          "end": 109.86,
          "en": "that use CodeSandbox",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.86,
          "end": 112.41,
          "en": "so that you can use that environment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.41,
          "end": 115.77000000000001,
          "en": "and that you can follow along throughout the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.77000000000001,
          "end": 118.473,
          "en": "without installing anything locally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.52000000000001,
          "end": 124.44,
          "en": "But, of course, you might also prefer a local React project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.44,
          "end": 129.24,
          "en": "instead of using this CodeSandbox in browser environment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.24,
          "end": 132.81,
          "en": "because creating such a local React project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.81,
          "end": 134.97,
          "en": "which runs on your machine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.97,
          "end": 137.22,
          "en": "of course, gives you the advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.22,
          "end": 140.91,
          "en": "that you can configure it exactly to your needs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.91,
          "end": 144.24,
          "en": "that you can use your favorite code editor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.24,
          "end": 146.79,
          "en": "for example, Visual Studio Code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.79,
          "end": 151.05,
          "en": "a very popular code editor which is totally free to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.05,
          "end": 155.73,
          "en": "and which is available for all major operating systems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.73,
          "end": 158.52,
          "en": "and which therefore is the code editor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.52,
          "end": 161.73,
          "en": "I'll suggest for following along with this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.73,
          "end": 165.18,
          "en": "if you do go for a local project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.18,
          "end": 167.28,
          "en": "because in that code editor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.28,
          "end": 170.52,
          "en": "you can then set up everything the way you want it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.52,
          "end": 172.59,
          "en": "install extra extensions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.59,
          "end": 175.5,
          "en": "that make your life as a developer easier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.5,
          "end": 179.88,
          "en": "and therefore you might prefer having such a local project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 179.88,
          "end": 184.44,
          "en": "instead of that web-based project CodeSandbox gives you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.44,
          "end": 187.92,
          "en": "But if you want to create such a local project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.92,
          "end": 192.92,
          "en": "you'll need to also install NodeJS from nodejs.org.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 194.46,
          "end": 199.26,
          "en": "And there you can download the latest or the LTS version,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 199.26,
          "end": 200.91,
          "en": "that's up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 200.91,
          "end": 204.45,
          "en": "because even though this is not a NodeJS course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 204.45,
          "end": 209.19,
          "en": "and you won't write any NodeJS code throughout this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 209.19,
          "end": 214.19,
          "en": "you need NodeJS because these different tools like Vite,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 214.29,
          "end": 218.88,
          "en": "which you can use for creating local React projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 218.88,
          "end": 221.64,
          "en": "under the hood use NodeJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 221.64,
          "end": 225.18,
          "en": "So you need NodeJS for these tools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 225.18,
          "end": 226.65,
          "en": "And speaking of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 226.65,
          "end": 229.41,
          "en": "there are different tools you could use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 229.41,
          "end": 232.95,
          "en": "to create such local React projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 232.95,
          "end": 235.65,
          "en": "Vite is an extremely popular one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 235.65,
          "end": 238.95,
          "en": "but if you search for create React project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 238.95,
          "end": 242.94,
          "en": "you'll, for example, also find Create React App,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 242.94,
          "end": 245.07,
          "en": "which is an alternative to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 245.07,
          "end": 248.07,
          "en": "so another tool which you could also look into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 248.07,
          "end": 250.77,
          "en": "to create React projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 250.77,
          "end": 255.33,
          "en": "And both these tools in the end give you simple commands",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 255.33,
          "end": 258.963,
          "en": "that you can execute to create new projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 260.01,
          "end": 262.02,
          "en": "For example, when using Vite,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 262.02,
          "end": 266.22,
          "en": "you have to run npm create vite@latest",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 266.22,
          "end": 271.22,
          "en": "in your command prompt or terminal after installing NodeJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 271.71,
          "end": 274.59000000000003,
          "en": "and this will then ask you a couple of questions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 274.59000000000003,
          "end": 277.71,
          "en": "where you can then choose that you want to create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 277.71,
          "end": 279.153,
          "en": "a React project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 280.26,
          "end": 282.45,
          "en": "And as a result, you'll get a project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 282.45,
          "end": 286.62,
          "en": "which you can open up with any code editor of your choice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 286.62,
          "end": 289.59000000000003,
          "en": "for example, as mentioned, Visual Studio Code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 289.59000000000003,
          "end": 292.413,
          "en": "and you can get started working on that code there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 293.52,
          "end": 297.54,
          "en": "One important note about these local projects, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 297.54,
          "end": 301.38,
          "en": "there, whenever you first create such a project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 301.38,
          "end": 303.81,
          "en": "you have to run npm install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 303.81,
          "end": 308.73,
          "en": "to install all extra packages that are used by that project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 308.73,
          "end": 312.063,
          "en": "for example, the React library package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 313.17,
          "end": 316.92,
          "en": "And then thereafter, in case of Vite projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 316.92,
          "end": 320.67,
          "en": "you have to run npm run dev in a terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 320.67,
          "end": 323.01,
          "en": "to start up a development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 323.01,
          "end": 324.69,
          "en": "which allows you to visit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 324.69,
          "end": 328.23,
          "en": "and preview the website you are working on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 328.23,
          "end": 331.14,
          "en": "And you should keep that server up and running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 331.14,
          "end": 333.93,
          "en": "as long as you are working on your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 333.93,
          "end": 337.11,
          "en": "because this underlying server process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 337.11,
          "end": 339.87,
          "en": "will also watch your code files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 339.87,
          "end": 342.57,
          "en": "and update that preview website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 342.57,
          "end": 345.633,
          "en": "whenever you save changes to your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 346.5,
          "end": 348.72,
          "en": "So this gives you a very efficient way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 348.72,
          "end": 352.803,
          "en": "of working on your code and seeing those changes in action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 353.67,
          "end": 355.32,
          "en": "Whenever you are done for the day,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 355.32,
          "end": 358.32,
          "en": "you can quit that process and then restart it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 358.32,
          "end": 360.783,
          "en": "whenever you're ready to pick up work again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 361.62,
          "end": 365.43,
          "en": "If you're using a CodeSandbox-based project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 365.43,
          "end": 368.37,
          "en": "you don't have to run npm install though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 368.37,
          "end": 372.75,
          "en": "and you don't have to run npm run dev or any other command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 372.75,
          "end": 376.38,
          "en": "Instead there, everything is already set up for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 376.38,
          "end": 379.44,
          "en": "you got your preview window on the right here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 379.44,
          "end": 381.69,
          "en": "you can adjust the UI as needed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 381.69,
          "end": 383.883,
          "en": "and you can dive right into the code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 384.84,
          "end": 389.34,
          "en": "But just as you find CodeSandbox-based starting projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 389.34,
          "end": 391.38,
          "en": "in all those course sections,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 391.38,
          "end": 396.38,
          "en": "I also always give you local project snapshots,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 396.72,
          "end": 399.39,
          "en": "zip files, to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 399.39,
          "end": 402.27,
          "en": "which you can download and extract",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 402.27,
          "end": 406.14,
          "en": "and which you could then open with your code editor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 406.14,
          "end": 411,
          "en": "to run npm install once after you first downloaded it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 411,
          "end": 415.05,
          "en": "and then npm run dev to work in that local project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 415.05,
          "end": 418.263,
          "en": "so you got both options throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 419.25,
          "end": 421.65,
          "en": "But why exactly do we need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 421.65,
          "end": 425.31,
          "en": "such a rather complex project setup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 425.31,
          "end": 428.943,
          "en": "if all we want to do is write some React code?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}